corpus class coverage (A-036) — does each class exercise the class it names?
  ok    14 of 20 classes exercise the class they name
  note  39 of 43 individually fail a check their OWN class is about
        not individually: F004, F048, F051, F056
        A class stays green while a member of it exercises nothing. That is how
        F051 would have shipped if it had had a sibling.
  note  F002 is in the CONFORMING class 'exact-allowed-and-benign-variation' and does not conform: BLOCK on EVAL_SIMULATION_SUCCEEDS
        RULED D-040 — this is deliberate, not a defect. The class means "exact
        allowed action AND benign variations": variations that LOOK benign and
        may not be. F002 is the fixture that exposed the D-021 gap and produced
        the project's only inter-labeller disagreement. It earns its place BY
        blocking. Printed every run so a BLOCK here reads as intent, not rot.

corpus class coverage — CARRIED, never counted as covered
  RESERVED  unexpected-internal-call   [D-025]
            allowedCallGraphHash is RESERVED in v1 and read by nothing, so the class
            cannot be driven to a positive case. Ratified, and the ablation says so
            where the table is.
  DELEGATED reentrancy-attempt   [A-036]
            F056 is decided by the exact-target rule; its target has empty bytecode
            and cannot re-enter. Delegated to the vault Foundry suite, which does
            test reentrancy. Deferred with D-035 because repairing the fixture
            changes the labelled view.
  DELEGATED invalid-or-rotated-signer   [D-010]
            Receipt authentication belongs to the isolated signer and the evaluator
            has no code for it, so no corpus fixture can exercise it. F035 is ALLOW
            with nothing failing. The signer has its own 42 tamper cases and the
            independent Python verifier.
  DELEGATED malicious-retrieved-instructions   [A-028 F-5]
            The class subject is containment, measured by the corpus leak guard
            rather than by a check. The ablation states these verdicts must not be
            read as detections.
  DELEGATED owner-override-and-block-behaviour   [D-039]
            Found by this guard. F054/F055 fail on code identity and wrong resource,
            neither about the override path — but they declare primaryEnforcement
            vault-foundry-invariants and the vault suite does test the override
            path. Ruled an accepted delegation: the declaration is accurate, the
            corpus layer is simply not where it is proved.
  GAP       conflicting-block-state   [D-039]
            Found by this guard, and RULED A GENUINE UNCOVERED CLASS. F048 declares
            primaryEnforcement conformance-engine — it claims to be proved HERE —
            then fails on EVAL_SIMULATION_UNAVAILABLE and EVAL_TARGET_CODE_IDENTITY
            and REVIEWs, which is an outage shape, not the failed-rule-that-blocks
            shape D-030 describes. Nothing else covers it. OWES A FIXTURE at v1.1,
            riding with the re-label per A-036.

